?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -7.62, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 4.0, "poll_sd": 10.24, "poll_weight": 0.2, "fundamentals": {"margin": -2.72, "lean": -8.0, "environment": 8.2, "incumbency": -2.0, "money": -0.92}, "rating_margin": -10.89, "sigma_race": 6.5, "sigma_total": 7.28, "baseline_margin": -5.3, "analyst_adjustment": 0.3, "key_factors": ["A strongly Democratic national environment nearly offsets the district's R+8 partisan lean", "An August Hendrix College poll of likely voters showed Jones leading Hill by four points, the only recent independent survey", "Hill holds a decisive money advantage: $3.0 million on hand to Jones's $191,000, plus outside support", "Expert ratings (six of nine at Likely R or better) and Polymarket pricing (~17% for Jones) still favor Republicans"], "rationale": "A credible August poll and a Democratic-favorable midterm environment make this central Arkansas seat genuinely competitive despite its Republican lean, and Jones has attracted national attention and Democratic targeting. But Hill's incumbency, dominant fundraising, and the weight of expert ratings and market pricing keep him favored, landing the race as Lean R with real upside for Jones if the polling holds.", "watch": "Whether post-Labor Day surveys confirm Jones's standing or Hill's spending advantage and the district's Republican baseline reassert themselves in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent French Hill (R) is running."]}, "overview": "This central Arkansas district leans Republican by about eight points, but a favorable national environment for Democrats has put the seat in play. Challenger Chris Jones has drawn endorsements from Kamala Harris, Pete Buttigieg, and Joe Kennedy III, and House Democrats added the district to their target list. An August Hendrix College poll of likely voters showed Jones leading French Hill by four points, and a Democratic-sponsored survey in May showed a similar narrow edge.\n\nHill retains the traditional advantages: he has raised $4.4 million to Jones's $1.2 million, held nearly $3 million on hand at mid-year, and benefits from outside group support. Most expert ratings still call the race Likely or Solid Republican, and prediction markets price Jones's chances at roughly one in six. Hill enters the final stretch favored by about five points, with genuine room for an upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}]}